storyDescription:
As an AdminPro portal user,I want to navigate to a dedicated "About" page,So that I can view system information, current application versioning, and the core team behind the platform.Description & ScopeWe are introducing a completely new, static view to the application: the About Page. This story covers the frontend implementation of the page template, the integration into the existing sidebar navigation menu, and populating the page sections using local mock data.No backend services are required; all text details and team data will be hardcoded via a mock constants file.UI & Design SpecificationsNavigation Link: Add an "About" item to the left-hand sidebar navigation (below "Settings") featuring an information icon (e.g., info or question-mark SVG).Page Layout: Standard page wrapper matching the dashboard width, containing:Application Overview Header: Simple card showing the system name, current build version, and last updated timestamp.Team Profiles Grid: A multi-column flex/grid section displaying core team contributors with placeholder avatar icons.Mock Data Payload (Frontend Implementation)Isolate this application and team metadata in a localized file (src/mock/aboutData.js):JSON{
  "systemInfo": {
    "appName": "AdminPro Portal",
    "version": "v2.4.0-stable",
    "environment": "Production Mock Environment",
    "lastUpdated": "May 2026"
  },
  "teamMembers": [
    {"id": 1, "name": "Sarah Jenkins", "role": "Lead Architect", "initials": "SJ"},
    {"id": 2, "name": "Michael Chang", "role": "Frontend Engineer", "initials": "MC"},
    {"id": 3, "name": "Elena Rostova", "role": "UI/UX Designer", "initials": "ER"}
  ]
}
Acceptance Criteria[ ] Routing & Navigation: A new route (/about) is registered in the application router. Clicking the "About" link in the sidebar successfully transitions the user to this page.[ ] Sidebar Visual State: The "About" item highlights when active, maintaining visual parity with how the "Dashboard" tab looks when selected.[ ] System Summary Card: The app name, version ($v2.4.0\text{-stable}$), and update details render cleanly at the top of the page.[ ] Team Grid Component: The teamMembers array maps correctly, rendering cards with the member's initials avatar, full name, and professional role.[ ] Responsive Fluidity: The layout stacks vertically on tablet/mobile views and spreads cleanly into columns on standard desktop resolutions.

